.TH BOARD-TUNE 1 "November 2026" "board-tune 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
board-tune \- configure Linux boards over SSH or through offline boot media
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B board-tune
.RI [ TARGET ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure a Raspberry Pi through an interactive Kconfig menu or saved profiles.
TARGET can be a user@host SSH destination, a whole removable disk, a disk image,
or an extracted root filesystem directory.
Changes are previewed before confirmation and affected files are backed up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--load " FILE
Load a Kconfig profile. Repeat to merge profiles. Without --menu, use batch mode.
.TP
.BI "--set " SYMBOL=VALUE
Override one configuration value.
.TP
.BI "--save " FILE
Export the minimal configuration.
.TP
.B --menu
Open the interactive menu after loading profiles.
.TP
.BR -n ", " --dry-run
Show planned changes without applying them.
.TP
.BR -y ", " --yes
Apply planned changes without the final confirmation.
.TP
.B --list-backups
List file backups on TARGET.
.TP
.BI "--restore " ID
Preview and restore a file backup. Combine with --dry-run to inspect only.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the program version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B BOARD_TUNE_PATH
is a colon-separated list of extra hook and platform directories.
.SH FILES
.I /var/backups/board-tune
contains private snapshots on the target, including original file contents
and metadata. Backups do not undo runtime effects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR lsblk (8),
.BR losetup (8)
.PP
Additional documentation is installed under /usr/share/doc/board-tune.
